From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoreXGT <aulia.ikbal09@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:20:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] init: always boot permissive on all build variants (cm-13.0)

cm-13.0 port of the cm-14.1 patch of the same name.

selinux_is_enforcing() returned true for user builds (ALLOW_DISABLE_SELINUX
is only honoured when the kernel cmdline asks for it), so init forced the
kernel into enforcing right at startup. Nikel's sepolicy is incomplete for
the MTK partitions, so a user build stalls in early-init mount_all and
never leaves the MI logo. Return false unconditionally so every variant
boots with androidboot.selinux=permissive from LK.

Also bump the init environment array from 32 to 64 entries: some MTK
services (e.g. ril-daemon-mtk) require a very large number of sockets,
which does not fit in 32 entries minus the other variables.

Change-Id: I5bd86e4745e4a32530e5972112cac891e0b2cae9
---
 init/init.cpp | 11 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/init/init.cpp b/init/init.cpp
--- a/init/init.cpp
+++ b/init/init.cpp
@@ -86,6 +86,9 @@ static char console_name[PROP_VALUE_MAX] = "/dev/console";
 static time_t process_needs_restart;
 
-static const char *ENV[32];
+/* nikel: some MTK services (e.g. ril-daemon-mtk) require very large number
+ * of sockets, which can't be contained in 32 entries minus other variables.
+ */
+static const char *ENV[64];
 
 bool waiting_for_exec = false;
 
@@ -927,12 +930,12 @@ static selinux_enforcing_status selinux_status_from_cmdline() {
     return false;
 }
 
 static bool selinux_is_enforcing(void)
 {
-    if (ALLOW_DISABLE_SELINUX) {
-        return selinux_status_from_cmdline() == SELINUX_ENFORCING;
-    }
-    return true;
+    /* nikel cm-13.0: always boot permissive for all variants
+     * (this tree's SELinux policy is incomplete; enforcing on user
+     * builds wedges the boot at early-init mount_all). */
+    return false;
 }
 
 int selinux_reload_policy(void)
